@startuml domain-billing
' Report §2.4 — Billing bounded context in full. The classes come from
' include/domain-billing.iuml, the same source the overview (domain-model.puml) uses.
!pragma layout smetana
!include include/style.iuml
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members

title Billing context (payment-service) — domain model

!include include/domain-billing.iuml
!include include/domain-published-language.iuml
!$only = "billing"
!include include/domain-event-links.iuml

remove @unlinked
hide <<DomainEvent>> members

note top of PaymentOrder
  <b>Invariants</b>
  · amount is more than zero
  · one order per registration (unique column);
    a redelivered request returns the existing order
  · charged only while PENDING
  · past holdExpiresAt: FAILED with reason
    HOLD_EXPIRED, gateway never called
end note

note bottom of PaymentGateway
  Domain port. Its adapter, SimulatedPaymentGateway
  (infrastructure), is deterministic by token:
  TOK_OK → SUCCEEDED
  TOK_TIMEOUT → TIMED_OUT, "GATEWAY_TIMEOUT"
  anything else → DECLINED, "CARD_DECLINED"
end note

legend right
  Value objects are Java records; Money and CardToken
  are JPA @Embeddable. Money is duplicated from the
  Registration context on purpose.
  PaymentStatus.REFUNDED exists, but no use case on
  main sets it (FR-11).
endlegend
@enduml
